  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) a reference value (zero in this case), (2) computation of differences between outcomes and the reference value (i.e., the outcomes themselves), and (3) evaluation of the expected differences (weighted by probabilities) to determine which lottery has the more favorable mean difference. The individual does not mention the reference value, nor do they compute or refer to differences from zero or expected values. Instead, they base their choice on the absolute monetary amount and a subjective assessment of probability differences. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason as defined. The reasoning is inconsistent with the structure of the decision reason, which involves a formal comparison of mean differences from a reference point. The individual’s justification is based on a different rule: preferring the higher guaranteed amount when probabilities are similar, which is not equivalent to the mean difference rule described in the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
